{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0e91bab534b266da92e6cb92c6ecf7bcdcf4cf4bd8b5554a8190ca4fa7f35a87"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A suggested setup section recommends LM Studio plus the Continue.dev extension, with example JSON configuration pointing at a local LM Studio server endpoint."},{"claim_ids":["clm_155b54e42ba9e4dcc9b4769a83e6b7894597f96b6f35e4e7619ca7f88e186dba"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The models section lists code LLMs such as CodeLlama, WizardCoder, Starcoder, SantaCoder, Qwen 2.5 Coder, and DeepSeek R1 with sizes, languages, and release dates."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1c1854f16b49dcba881a6098cda0f3ee40ff1c3a823744f9e75e890e7248cb4f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The chat interfaces section lists tools with shell/REPL/notebook access, including open-interpreter, gptme, and octogen."},{"claim_ids":["clm_391a238894c6410c5157985a8ace16abb916ee7823dac10c4ddcf6b8c3e522ad"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tools section lists project/feature-generation tools including gpt-engineer, gpt-pilot, aider, rift, mentat, and Refact.AI with star counts and notes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_417b4269e5846902183e65ee4916d4470dc12e42bafed1de2193211bb615bd35"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors are invited to keep the list up to date by editing data/data.yaml via the repository's edit link."},{"claim_ids":["clm_61b7216f930223139ddd1f353dd5469f727dae1e9d66b7de3fcfd474692b26ce"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The document itself notes that local copilots' output quality is not yet on par with cloud services like GitHub Copilot, and that the models section is expected to become out of date quickly."},{"claim_ids":["clm_76b3f6be2f7eaa4b9bd102e30defda65b299936f2e1847e593b2b53bc7ce90c1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The editor extensions section is a table listing tools such as Tabby, Fauxpilot, turbopilot, localpilot, and Cursor with editor support, star counts, release dates, and notes."},{"c